  "description": "The control socket clause (Tu, 2026-09-27). A worker closes a connection's control socket only after that connection's connection_lost, or by exiting — never to shed a slow core: session model §9 E9 reads a control socket that closes without connection_lost as the worker's death, which ends every session on it terminated / worker_lost. Here the first core stops reading for a while (backpressure — the worker stops reading the target — never a hang-up), and then closes its control socket without disconnect: the graceful restart. The worker ends nothing; the next core reattaches and finds the session live.",
  "corpus": [
    "session model §9 E9",
    "immortality §2.1",
    "phase-01 (manage.sh restart-core)"
  ],
